Let $k$ be a field and let $n>2$ be an integer. Consider the polynomial ring $k[x_1,\dots,x_n]$ and its automorphism group $\mathrm{GA}_n(k)$, consisting of $k$-algebra automorphisms of $k[x_1,\dots,x_n]$ (equivalently, polynomial automorphisms of affine $n$-space $\mathbb{A}^n_k$). Inside $\mathrm{GA}_n(k)$ define:
\begin{itemize}
\item the affine subgroup $\mathrm{Aff}_n(k)$, consisting of automorphisms $(x_1,\dots,x_n)\mapsto (L_1,\dots,L_n)$ where each $L_i$ is a polynomial of total degree $\le 1$;
\item the triangular (de Jonquières) subgroup $\mathrm{BA}_n(k)$, consisting of automorphisms of the form $x_i\mapsto a_i x_i + f_i(x_{i+1},\dots,x_n)$ with $a_i\in k^\times$ and $f_i\in k[x_{i+1},\dots,x_n]$;
\item the tame subgroup $\mathrm{TA}_n(k)=\langle \mathrm{Aff}_n(k),\mathrm{BA}_n(k)\rangle$.
\end{itemize}
Determine whether $\mathrm{Aff}_n(k)$ is a maximal subgroup of $\mathrm{TA}_n(k)$; that is, whether there exists no subgroup $H$ with $\mathrm{Aff}_n(k)\subsetneq H\subsetneq \mathrm{TA}_n(k)$.

